    "density_scale_consumers": "The tagged public all-component-densities wrapper extracts get-density-config then passes the result to component density mixins. Component mixins pass the returned value to token density functions; checkbox tokens call clamp-density($config,-3). clamp-density maps only minimum/maximum or unitless numbers to scales and returns 0 for any other type. The same finite owned helper and checkbox token path show this scalar scale model.",
    "no_map_use_examples": "A scoped search of the archived Material 16 SCSS files found no call site supplying a literal density configuration Map. Every relevant theme path extracts the density map entry into a scale slot; the public all-density mixin forwards that scale into scalar scale consumers.",
    "tagged_public_doc": "Material 16.2.14 core/theming/_theming.scss documents $theme-or-config, $default and return all as Map. The public _index.scss forwards get-density-config. This is the old public SassDoc annotation, but it does not distinguish a Map theme wrapper from the actual density scalar.",
    "theme_shape": "Material 16 define-light-theme/define-dark-theme accept a theme container Map. private-is-theme-object classifies maps with color/density/typography keys or empty map as themes. Therefore Map remains a valid input type for the wrapper/theme argument.",
    "upstream_doc_correction": "The independently authenticated change for SHA 3ea64a90... changes only SassDoc: input becomes Map | String | Number; default and return become String | Number. Function body and signature do not change. Its scope is correction of docs, not implementation."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Public consumer compilation was run only against the immutable tagged Material 16 artifact. The owned helper plus owned clamp-density were separately compiled and match, but the frozen full owned public index references an unavailable current Material override mixin in this context, so the full owned checkbox stylesheet was not treated as validated.",
    "No CSS golden, full bundle, component theme suite, output artifact, or browser was produced.",
    "The conclusion concerns supported theme/density-scale contract. Arbitrary downstream custom functions could intentionally use get-density-config pass-through for a Map, but no such usage is documented or found in the owned/tagged callsites reviewed."
  ],
  "recommendation": {
    "conservative_note": "The old tagged SassDoc incorrectly says Map for all three positions and is itself public documentation; the exact subsequent upstream fix plus consumer evidence supports correcting default/return while preserving Map for theme input. If preserving literal compatibility with old generated docs is a requirement beyond the public behavior contract, the narrow fallback is Map | String | Number for return\u2014but this overstates the behavior that actual density mixins can meaningfully consume.",
    "default": "Use String | Number for the default density scale. A Map default passes through at runtime but has no mapped theme/component scale interpretation and therefore is not supported as the density default contract.",
    "public_input": "Keep Map in the $theme-or-config input union because a supported theme is a Map; document scalar direct density configurations as String | Number.",
    "return": "Use String | Number for the documented return contract. The Map returned by malformed/direct Map or map-valued density field is permissive behavior and collapses to scale 0 in a real tagged public component consumer. Do not alter that permissive runtime behavior in this documentation-only change."
  },
